# Cape Town (the owner, 17.10.2026: "B and a little lower, Gansbaai"): the 1 km box from Saldanha
# and Langebaan past the Peninsula, False Bay, the mountains east, Hermanus to Gansbaai and Danger
# Point, 117 x 249 km, turned 17° (north end west): Lambert true at 33.5-34.5 S (southern
# hemisphere), its meridian 30.4° west of the box.
NAME="Cape Town"
REF_LAT=-33.811
REF_LON=18.655
TRUELAT1=-33.5
TRUELAT2=-34.5
STAND_LON=-11.75
E_WE="100, 82, 118, 67"
E_SN="100, 109, 250, 73"
I_PARENT="1, 40, 13, 53"
J_PARENT="1, 33, 13, 35"
# A second 1 km box beside the first (the owner, 02.11.2026: "one interesting place ... where usually everyone go when
# it is no wind in capetown, but there you can catch thermal winds"): the Breede valley from Brandvlei Dam and Worcester
# to Robertson, 66 x 72 km, one 3 km cell east of the main box (boxes at one level may not overlap); the 3 km box
# widened east (64 -> 82) to hold it with 21 km to spare. Both 1 km boxes are the 3 km one's (PARENT_ID, WPS numbering).
PARENT_ID="1, 1, 2, 2"
GFS_TOP=-28
GFS_BOTTOM=-40
GFS_LEFT=12
GFS_RIGHT=26
POINT_NAME="Bloubergstrand (Kite Beach)"
POINT_LAT=-33.80
POINT_LON=18.46
